/-!
# A cartesian module presheaf on a big affine site is a sheaf

Let `S` be a scheme and let `𝓕` be a presheaf of `𝒪_Aff`-modules on one of the big affine sites
`(Aff/S)_τ` of Stacks 0GZV which is *cartesian*: all of its base-change comparisons
`𝓕(U') ⊗_{𝒪(U')} 𝒪(U) ⟶ 𝓕(U)` are isomorphisms. Then `𝓕` satisfies the sheaf axiom for `τ`.

This is the **sheaf conjunct** of conditions (2)–(6) of Stacks 0GZV, deduced from condition (1),
for all five of `τ` Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic and fppf; the source gets it from Algebra,
Lemma 10.24.1 for the Zariski topology and from the chain of equivalences for the others, while
here it is flat descent of modules, Stacks 023M, applied directly at each topology: a standard
`τ`-covering of an affine scheme by affine schemes is faithfully flat on global functions and
its double overlaps are fibre products of affine schemes, hence pushouts of rings.

The base's `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherentModulesAndAffines` proves the
*quasi-coherence* conjunct of (2)–(6) from condition (1) for all five topologies, but takes its
module already given as a sheaf; this file supplies the conjunct that was missing there.

## Main results

* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.faithfullyFlat_pi_schemeGamma` and
  `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isPushout_schemeGamma`: the presheaf of global functions of a functor
  to affine schemes is faithfully flat along a finite flat covering family and turns fibre
  products into pushouts of rings.
* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_schemeGamma`: **a cartesian presheaf of modules
  over the presheaf of global functions is a sheaf**, for a topology generated by finite flat
  covering families of affine schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppf_covering_flat` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppf_covering_finite_flat`: the covering families of `(Aff/S)_fppf`
  are finite and flat on the underlying schemes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineZariski_covering_flat` and its étale, smooth and syntomic
  counterparts: the same for the other four big affine sites.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppf_isSheaf_of_cartesian`: Stacks 0GZV, condition (1) implies the
  sheaf conjunct of condition (6).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineZariski_isSheaf_of_cartesian`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineEtale_isSheaf_of_cartesian`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineSmooth_isSheaf_of_cartesian` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineSyntomic_isSheaf_of_cartesian`: Stacks 0GZV, condition (1) implies
  the sheaf conjunct of each of conditions (2)–(5).

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_of_flat_covers'` is stated for an arbitrary
presheaf of rings together with the two facts about it that its proof uses. Those two facts are
discharged here once and for all for the presheaf `L.op ⋙ Scheme.Γ` of global functions, from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.faithfullyFlat_pi_appTop` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPushout_appTop_of_isPullback`; no universe lift of the sections of the
structure presheaf is needed, unlike in the `Stacks.Sites.liftedSchemeRings` form of those
statements. The structure presheaf of `AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppfRingedSite` *is*
`L.op ⋙ Scheme.Γ` for `L` the functor to schemes, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppfRingedSite_O_obj`, so the statement is about the structure
presheaf that ringed site carries.

The sections of the module presheaf live in `Type (max m u)` for a free universe `m`, where `u`
is the universe of the schemes, so that `m := u` gives the sections in `Type u` — the universe
in which conditions (1)–(8) of Stacks 0GZV are stated throughout this development, and so the
universe at which the sheaf conjunct proved here composes with the quasi-coherence conjunct of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherentModulesAndAffines`. That composition is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.BigAffineSitePresheafConditions`.

There is no size condition relating the sections to the objects of the site, which live in
`Type (u + 1)`. The transport of the sheaf axiom along the forgetful functor to types is in the
direction types-to-groups only, `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp`, which needs
no limits in the category of sections; that is what
`Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_of_flat_covers'` supplies over
`Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_of_flat_covers`, whose use of
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_comp` forces the sections to be at least as large
as the objects. The same primed statement is what puts the Stacks 0GZX sheaf conjunct,
`AlgebraicGeometry.smallAffineEtale_isSheaf_of_baseChange_isIso`, at sections in `Type u`.

## Coverage limits

All five members of the family are done, each from its own standard-covering predicate: the
Zariski one through the open immersions of a standard Zariski covering, the étale, smooth and
syntomic ones through the étale, smooth and syntomic morphisms of the chosen big site's covering
families. Only the direction from condition (1) is proved here, and only this needs proving: the
sheaf conjunct of each of (2)–(6) is one of its own hypotheses, so there is no converse to it.
The converse of the *other* conjunct — each of conditions (2)–(6) back to condition (1) — is
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppf_isIso_canonicalMap_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` and its four
counterparts in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.BigAffineSiteQuasicoherentCartesian`,
which uses the covering predicates proved here through
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigAffineFppf_covering_flat` and its four counterparts.

